---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Meditate on Sri Yantra — Bindu Trataka, Sound & Mantras"
  description="Master the art of Sri Yantra meditation: Step-by-step Bindu Trataka gaze technique, 136.1 Hz Om cosmic octave resonance, and sacred seed mantras."
  canonicalPath="/meditation/"
  isDark={false}
>
  <Header isDark={false} />

  <main class="article-page">
    <article class="article-container">
      <header class="article-header">
        <div class="category-tag">Meditation Practice & Neuroscience</div>
        <h1 class="display-title article-title">
          How to Meditate on the Sri Yantra: The Complete Bindu Trataka & Mantra Guide
        </h1>
        <p class="article-subtitle">
          Discover how fixed-gaze meditation on the sacred center point quiets the Default Mode Network, balances brain hemispheres, and attunes consciousness with 136.1 Hz cosmic sound.
        </p>

        <div class="author-meta">
          <span>By <strong>Atharva Mahamuni</strong> (<a href="https://x.com/athmatwt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@athmatwt</a>)</span>
          <span class="meta-dot">•</span>
          <span>10 Min Read</span>
          <span class="meta-dot">•</span>
          <span>Practical Guide</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="article-content">
        <p class="lead-paragraph">
          Meditating on the Sri Yantra is not passive relaxation—it is an ancient technology of conscious visual entrainment called <strong>Bindu Trataka</strong> (fixed-gaze contemplation). When paired with rhythmic breathing and the 136.1 Hz primordial Om vibration, it systematically stills saccadic eye movement and silences the wandering mind.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Step-by-Step Bindu Trataka Practice</h2>
        <ol class="steps-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Set Your Posture:</strong> Sit comfortably with an upright, relaxed spine. Position your screen or altar at eye level, roughly 2 to 3 feet (arm's length) away.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Soften Your Vision:</strong> Rather than hard staring, adopt a gentle, soft gaze. Look directly at the central golden point (the <em>Bindu</em>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Synchronize with the Prana Pulse:</strong> Follow our 16-second tidal breathing rhythm: 4 seconds gentle inhale, 4 seconds calm hold, 4 seconds soft exhale, 4 seconds resting stillness.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Natural Blinking:</strong> Blink naturally whenever necessary. Avoid straining your eyes. As concentration deepens, the urge to blink will naturally recede.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Observe Visual Phosphenes:</strong> Within 3 to 5 minutes, you may notice the outer triangles appearing to glow, pulsate, or shift dimensionally. Do not chase these optical effects; remain anchored at the Bindu.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <h2>2. Two Sacred Pathways: Srishti vs Samhara Krama</h2>
        <div class="comparison-grid">
          <div class="comp-card">
            <h3>Samhara Krama (Inward Dissolution)</h3>
            <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Mental stillness, ego dissolution, stress relief.</p>
            <p>
              Begin your gaze at the outermost square perimeter (the <em>Bhupura</em>). Mentally travel inward through the 16 and 8 lotus petals, journey through the 43 interlocking triangles, and rest completely absorbed in the dimensionless central Bindu.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="comp-card">
            <h3>Srishti Krama (Outward Expansion)</h3>
            <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Creative insight, manifestation, mental clarity.</p>
            <p>
              Begin with laser focus on the central Bindu. As your breath expands, allow your awareness to radiate outward through the triangles and lotus petals into the physical world, visualizing positive manifestation in your daily life.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="sound-physics">3. Acoustic Science of the 136.1 Hz Om Frequency</h2>
        <p>
          Why do we tune our procedural meditation engine to <strong>136.10 Hz</strong>?
        </p>
        <p>
          In 1978, Swiss mathematician and musicologist <strong>Hans Cousto</strong> formulated the law of the "Cosmic Octave"—a mathematical system for transposing planetary orbital periods into audible acoustic frequencies.
        </p>
        <div class="formula-box">
          <code>Frequency = [ 1 / (365.2422 days × 86,400 sec) ] × 2³² ≈ 136.10 Hz (C#₃)</code>
        </div>
        <p>
          This frequency corresponds to the musical note <strong>C#3</strong> (tuning A = 432 Hz), which is identical to the root tone <em>Sadja (Sa)</em> in traditional Indian classical music. Frequencies in this 100–140 Hz window physically resonate in the thoracic and neck cavities, stimulating the auricular branch of the <strong>vagus nerve</strong> to trigger deep parasympathetic nervous system recovery.
        </p>

        <h2 id="mantras">4. Sacred Mantras of the Sri Yantra</h2>
        <p>
          Sound and geometry are complementary vibrations. While the Sri Yantra is the visual yantra, these mantras provide the auditory resonance:
        </p>

        <div class="mantra-showcase">
          <div class="mantra-entry">
            <div class="mantra-devanagari">श्रीं (SHREEM)</div>
            <div class="mantra-name">The Bija (Seed) Mantra of Prosperity and Light</div>
            <p>Chanted in rhythm with your breathing: "Shreeeee-m". Represents radiant cosmic abundance and feminine grace.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mantra-entry">
            <div class="mantra-devanagari">ॐ ऐं ह्रीं श्रीं श्री मात्रे नमः</div>
            <div class="mantra-name">The Universal Sri Matre Maha Mantra</div>
            <p><em>"Om Aim Hreem Shreem Sri Matre Namah"</em> — Salutations to the Divine Mother of the Sacred Geometry. Brings wisdom (Aim), transformation (Hreem), and spiritual abundance (Shreem).</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mantra-entry">
            <div class="mantra-devanagari">क ए ई ल ह्रीं • ह स क ह ल ह्रीं • स क ल ह्रीं</div>
            <div class="mantra-name">Panchadasakshari (The 15-Lettered Sri Vidya Code)</div>
            <p>The sacred 15 syllables mapping to the 3 sections of the human spine and the interlocking triangles of the Sri Yantra.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cta-box">
          <h3>Begin Your Trataka Session Now</h3>
          <p>
            Launch our fullscreen visualizer with 136.1 Hz Om drone and automatic Screen Wake Lock.
          </p>
          <a href="/" class="cta-btn">Start Fullscreen Meditation</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer isDark={false} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .article-page {
    padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;
    background-color: var(--color-canvas);
  }

  .article-container {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .article-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .category-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .article-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .article-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    color: var(--color-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .author-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }

  .meta-dot {
    color: var(--color-hairline-strong);
  }

  .article-content {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .lead-paragraph {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .steps-list {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .comparison-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 2.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .comparison-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .comp-card {
    background-color: var(--color-surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.75rem;
  }

  .comp-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .formula-box {
    background-color: var(--color-surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .mantra-showcase {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .mantra-entry {
    background-color: var(--color-surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .mantra-devanagari {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .mantra-name {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .cta-box {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    background-color: var(--color-surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 2.25rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-box h3 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .cta-btn {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background-color: var(--color-primary);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
